### course-service — example requests
# course/course-service-with-loco — "person-style" layout (src/api/rest/).
# Envelope: same as place/thing — data/error OMITTED (not null) on the
# unused side (#[serde(skip_serializing_if)]). Gated by
# COURSE_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off). No review-queue HTTP surface, no
# cross-service links, no bulk import/export for this crate.
#
# GOTCHA: `GET /api/courses` (bare list, no query) is unimplemented —
# it returns 501. Use /api/courses/search instead.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8086
@courseId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@instanceId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### Who am I — always requires a valid bearer token (curl-verified 401
# "missing authorization header" with none, regardless of
# COURSE_REQUIRE_AUTH — see person.http for the same pattern).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### GET /api/courses (bare list) — deliberately unimplemented, returns
# 501; included so you don't file it as a bug. Use search below instead.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses


### Create a course — minimal valid body (Course is heavily
# #[serde(default)]-annotated, person-style).
# @name createCourse
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Accepts-version: 1.0

{
  "name": "Intro to Widgets",
  "course_code": "TEST101",
  "status": "published"
}


### Get the created course back
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}


### Search courses — the response's array field is `items`, not
# `results`/`courses` (differs from every sibling crate).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/search?q=Widgets&limit=10


### Update a course
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Intro to Widgets (2026 edition)",
  "course_code": "TEST101",
  "status": "published"
}


### Probabilistic + deterministic match
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/match
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Intro to Widgets", "course_code": "TEST101", "status": "published" }


### Explicit duplicate check
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/check-duplicates
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Intro to Widgets", "course_code": "TEST101", "status": "published" }


### Batch deduplicate
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/deduplicate


### Merge two confirmed-duplicate courses (destructive)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/merge
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "main_id": "{{courseId}}", "duplicate_id": "<other-uuid>" }


### Create a course instance — a specific offering of this course
# (course_id in the body is required by the model, though the server
# also takes it from the path).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/instances
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{instanceId}}",
  "course_id": "{{courseId}}",
  "name": "Spring 2026",
  "status": "scheduled"
}


### List this course's instances
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/instances


### Get one instance
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/instances/{{instanceId}}


### Masked view
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/masked


### GDPR export
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/export


### Audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/audit


### FHIR — read this course as a Basic resource (no FHIR R5 resource
# models a course; Basic is the documented non-standard fallback,
# agents/share/fhir.md §3).
GET {{baseUrl}}/fhir/Basic/{{courseId}}


### Delete (soft-delete) a course
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}
